Guaji remained the largest population group, with Bayani and Kaftian communities still forming major minorities and Sartan / mixed families concentrated in urban business, media, and administrative circles. Growth in the 1980s and 1990s was strongest along the coast, in resort districts, and in the airport-linked corridors around the capital and northern beaches.

== Death of Mera ==

Mera remained president until April 14, 2000, when he died in office. By then, he had become the central figure of the long recovery era: publicly popular, internationally tolerated, and domestically controversial. His death ended the era of crisis management that had begun in 1976 and opened the next political transition.

